F2  MINOR — behaviour 3's reds are untagged: genuine evidence, not a hole
================================================================
studio/ci/reds/W-076/03.log's two failures carry no [W-076 b3] tag (0/2).
CAUSE, not a scoping hole: behaviour 3 is the only behaviour outside
packages/cli/src/check.test.ts. It lives in apps/server/test/server.test.ts,
whose pre-existing harness is check(name, cond, detail) — no behaviour-tag
parameter, unlike check.test.ts's checkB(n, ...). The builder could not tag
without editing that harness.

ATTRIBUTION IS NEVERTHELESS SOUND, on four independent grounds:
  1. the log header names it: "# behaviour: 3";
  2. the command is scoped to that one file:
     "node --import tsx apps/server/test/server.test.ts .";
  3. the two failing names are unique to this opus ("inbox body: at least
     2KB", "inbox body: byte-identical to the front matter body") — no other
     assertion in that file matches "inbox body";
  4. PROVENANCE: both failures report `undefined` for row.body, exactly the
     pre-store.ts state, and the sibling PASS line shows the pre-fix raw
     subject "**W-064's red gate: D-024's kill arm has fired, and only you
     can rule.**" — the old body.split("\n")[0]. Post-fix the same line
     prints the stripped derivation. The log cannot have been recorded after
     the implementation.
  5. Mutation M1 reproduced both failures verbatim, same names.
SINGLE INSTANCE. Searched all five red logs for behaviour-tagged lines;
01/02/04/05 are fully tagged (25/25, 2/2, 7/7, 13/13).

